Two compile blockers from GitHub Actions run 36102017287 (:app:compileDebugKotlin).

1. AtomicJson.kt — `AtomicJson.kt:67 Unresolved reference: exists`.
   `AtomicFile` has no `exists()`; the helper was declared on top of it and used
   as a pre-check in `read()`. Both are deleted. `readFully()` already throws
   `FileNotFoundException` for an absent file, which is the only legitimate
   `Missing` signal, so the check was both redundant and semantically worse: it
   duplicated a decision `AtomicFile` owns (its `.new` recovery sidecar) and read
   a stale `File.exists()` answer. Catching exactly one exception type keeps the
   contract three-valued — absent -> Missing, unreadable/truncated -> Corrupt,
   parse failure -> Corrupt. A damaged marker is still Corrupt, never Missing.

2. BackupManager.kt — `'public' function exposes its 'internal' parameter type
   RestoreFs` (x3). `RestoreFs` stays internal: it is the filesystem test seam
   for the restore protocol, not production API. The public facades are kept and
   supply `RealRestoreFs` themselves; every overload carrying `RestoreFs` in its
   signature becomes `internal`:
     - recoverInterruptedRestore(context, fs)
     - recoverInterruptedRestore(context, lifeDatabase, fs)
     - restore(..., hooks, fs)

No behaviour change beyond the two sites. Restore state machine, COMMITTED
semantics, startup barrier, media staging, Reference, Plan, Reading, Share and
Closet are untouched.
